{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Visiting the iniquity of fathers upon children.</b> He lengthens [His patience] until the fourth generation: if they uphold their fathers' deeds in their own hands and add further evil, their measure becomes full in the third generation, the hope of their repentance is lost, and they are punished. But if they uphold their fathers' deeds yet do not add further evil beyond them, He waits until the fourth generation — and then their measure becomes full with no hope of repentance remaining, and they perish."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:47.323879193Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}